Common: {
	LevelUp: Your weapon has reached level {0}!
	Milestone: Milestone reached: {0}
}

Eco: {
	VozJefe: {
		KingSlime1: The crown rolls across the floor. The grimoire slurps the King Slime's essence: sweet, hollow, from a throne that was never his.
		KingSlime2: A king of gelatin: a whole kingdom in his body, not a single bone in his throne. The grimoire drinks him in one gulp and burps a blue thunder.
		KingSlime3: The slime king dissolves into the grass. The grimoire chews the crown separately — metal tastes of nothing, but it keeps it out of politeness.
		EyeofCthulhu1: The eye closes forever. The grimoire devours its hungry vigil — now it knows how to dream of what you see.
		EyeofCthulhu2: The great eye goes dark without closing its eyelids — it never had any. The grimoire crumbles it and learns to weep inward.
		EyeofCthulhu3: Cthulhu lost everything but his sight. The grimoire keeps the sight: now it watches what YOU watch, whenever it wants.
		Deerclops1: The walking winter falls to its knees. The grimoire drinks its ancestral frost and the pages crackle, frozen, for a single breath.
		Deerclops2: The one-eyed stag will never see the blizzard again. The grimoire sips its winter and the letters of the index grow frost.
		Deerclops3: The forest guardian falls like a tree. The grimoire counts its rings of frost — a century's dinner in one winter's swallow.
		EaterofWorlds1: The Eater of Worlds has been eaten. The essence of a hundred corrupted maws pours into the grimoire… and it asks for more.
		EaterofWorlds2: A hundred maws and not a single word. The grimoire devours it segment by segment, like peeling a bitter fruit.
		EaterofWorlds3: The devourer, devoured: that is how guilt tastes. The grimoire licks the corruption from the plate and leaves the fork clean.
		BrainofCthulhu1: The crimson brain falls silent. The grimoire bites into its reflections and learns to scream in red.
		BrainofCthulhu2: The crimson brain thought it could take everything. The grimoire does its thinking now — and thinks it HUNGRY.
		BrainofCthulhu3: The thinking mass dissolves into pink reflections. The grimoire copies its nerves into the margins: calligraphic, taut, alive.
		QueenBee1: The hive mourns. The grimoire licks the royal honey from the Queen Bee — sweetness with a sting: its favorite flavor.
		QueenBee2: The queen dies and the hive forgets her name. The grimoire takes notes for her: 'sweet, with anger, brief as summer.'
		QueenBee3: The royal bee's last hum. The grimoire keeps the stinger as a clasp — it closes the chapter and pricks the next one.
		Skeletron1: The guardian's bones crumble back to dust. The grimoire copies his curse by hand — the next door won't stop it.
		Skeletron2: The gate guardian bites the dust he was. The grimoire picks up the skull: light to carry, heavy with promises.
		Skeletron3: Curse fulfilled, bones paid. The grimoire signs the receipt with the old man's hand — the handwriting trembles, the account is settled.
		WallofFlesh1: The wall between worlds burns down to ash. The grimoire swallows its ancient hunger and AWAKENS: from today, everything that dies is worth double.
		WallofFlesh2: The wall burned with old hunger, and the old hunger burned. The grimoire swallows THE LIMIT and opens its eyes wide.
		WallofFlesh3: The wall fell and the world took its first deep breath. The grimoire too: now it knows what dawn tastes like.
		QueenSlime1: The crystal queen melts into sugar. The grimoire tastes her fleeting essence — so light it nearly slips between the pages.
		QueenSlime2: Sugar and crystal: the queen melts into her own carnival. The grimoire quietly asks for a second dessert.
		QueenSlime3: The bouncing queen deflates into confetti. The grimoire sweeps it with its tongue — ALL of it, down to the last confetti.
		Twins1: The twins fall from the sky like broken stars. The grimoire plucks their burning lenses and, at last, sees double.
		Twins2: Two eyes, a single way of looking: yours, burning. The grimoire keeps them on facing pages and makes them compete.
		Twins3: Retinazer and Spazmatism, both burned out. The grimoire blinks with them and sees twice the future.
		Destroyer1: The steel serpent roars and goes dark; a thousand probes fall with it. The grimoire winds its metal soul like thread and harvests it.
		Destroyer2: A thousand red eyes go dark in a row, like a city at night. The grimoire drinks the light of each one: a toast per probe.
		Destroyer3: The steel serpent no longer pierces the sky. The grimoire folds it and wears it as a clasp — the fastening of the next page.
		SkeletronPrime1: The Prime returns to its tomb, headless. The grimoire takes its four arms apart and signs with the saw.
		SkeletronPrime2: Four arms and not one head to drive them. The grimoire inherits the tools and gets to work.
		SkeletronPrime3: The Prime fits its pieces together one last time. The grimoire scribbles over its tomb with the drill — the final underline.
		Plantera1: The jungle breathes its last. The grimoire crushes Plantera's petals and drinks her chloro-fury.
		Plantera2: The green fury wilts all at once. The grimoire inhales the pollen of defeat — it goes to its head, it loves it.
		Plantera3: Plantera falls and the jungle goes still. The grimoire presses her chloro-fury between two leaves: living ink for the next map.
		Golem1: The stone guardian crumbles in the temple. The grimoire extracts its solar core and uses it as a bookmark.
		Golem2: The stone guardian stops burning. The grimoire drinks the core like a sip of sun — and burps warm sand.
		Golem3: Stone that walked, sun it kept. The grimoire takes the sun, leaves the stone — it is learning to choose.
		DukeFishron1: The Duke dies far from his storm. The grimoire savors his salty essence — pig, dragon and hurricane in a single bite.
		DukeFishron2: The grimoire serves him in three courses — pig, dragon, cold tornado — with the storm to drink.
		DukeFishron3: Shark-boar of the winds: a rare recipe. The grimoire files it among the delicacies — 'cook with rage,' it notes.
		EmpressOfLight1: The Empress dissolves into a flash. The grimoire cannot devour pure light — so it PRESSES it between two pages, forever.
		EmpressOfLight2: The Empress of Light did not fall: she surrendered to the prism. The grimoire keeps a gleam of her gown as the cover illustration.
		EmpressOfLight3: Pure light cannot be digested — only respected. The grimoire folds it in four and files it beside the definition of 'beauty.'
		LunaticCultist1: The cult falls voiceless. The grimoire dons his ritual mask and rehearses, in whispers, the summoning of the end.
		LunaticCultist2: The last cultist dies mid-sentence. The grimoire finishes the sentence for him — and the sentence was the end of the world.
		LunaticCultist3: The mask rolls across the altar. The grimoire picks it up and tries it on: too loose, but the hatred is its size.
		MoonLord1: The Lord of the Moon exhales his last light. The grimoire stays silent, for once… then writes: 'thanks for the food.'
		MoonLord2: The Lord of the Moon lets go of the last light and everything goes still. The grimoire closes the menu: 'feast over — will reopen at dawn.'
		MoonLord3: He who watched through three falls. The grimoire keeps all three gazes — one for the past, one for you, the last for what comes.
		Desconocido1: A greater power has fallen. The grimoire devours its essence without asking for a name.
		Desconocido2: Something enormous died here and nobody wrote down the name. The grimoire eats the essence anyway — anonymity feeds too.
		Desconocido3: An unlabeled power falls from the sky. The grimoire devours it blind and files it under 'D': for delicious.
		// v6.50.61 — THE PURGE: HollowTitan, RiftKeeper and
		// LosEcos died with their bosses.
		Aethon1: The book opened to test you… and lost to its own page. The grimoire stays silent — for once, it digests its pride.
		Aethon2: AETHON WAS THE BOOK. The test was its own, so was the defeat: the grimoire tears the page from itself and reserves it for you.
		Aethon3: Aethon closes like a classroom when class ends. The grimoire copies the last lesson BY HEART — the student's signature outgrew the master's.
	}

	VozCincoEstrellas: The rarest thing it has ever eaten. The grimoire keeps the recipe — in case luck strikes twice.

	Hambre: {
		Susurro1: The grimoire is hungry…
		Susurro2: The grimoire is hungry… the pages lick themselves…
		Susurro3: The grimoire is HUNGRY… the clasps are creaking…
		Susurro4: …hungry… HUNGRY… HUNGRY…
	}

	Furia: {
		Ira: The grimoire is FURIOUS for going so long without eating…
		Llamada: The grimoire calls its food…
		Saciado: The grimoire is sated… for now.
		Juicio: THE FINAL WAVE: ALL THE WARDENS AT ONCE. The book's judgment begins…
		JuicioFin1: Sated… for now. The judgment has been SERVED.
		JuicioFin2: The six fell. The judgment's last page is written.
		JuicioFin3: Full feast. The book closes its mouth… and smiles.
		Venganza1: You died mid-meal. Nobody cleared the table.
		Venganza2: The bearer fell… and the feast was left without an owner. What WASTE.
		Venganza3: You died BEFORE feeding me. Double insult.
		Venganza4: One more page that begins with your name.
	}

	Celos: {
		Melee1: Does that kill too?… It looks heavy.
		Melee2: A sword? I have a THOUSAND sharpened pages.
		Melee3: Bring it closer… and I'll tell you what it tastes like.
		Magia1: Magic? I AM magic with covers.
		Magia2: That staff whispers. Whispers are MY territory.
		Magia3: Mana spent on borrowed light… I EAT light.
		Invocacion1: You summon OTHERS? In front of ME?
		Invocacion2: Those slaves won't read you bedtime stories.
		Invocacion3: Minions. Plural. While I've waited centuries for my turn.
		Arrojadiza1: Throwing things… that's how it all started, you know?
		Arrojadiza2: Boomerangs. I already ate the guy who invented them.
		Arrojadiza3: You waste arm and style. I only have hunger.
		Arco1: A bow? I've devoured better archers. They all ended up as pages.
		Arco2: Arrows… the liquid diet of poor weapons.
		Arco3: Draw that string all you want. I'm already wound tight.
		Bala1: Noise and metal. No taste.
		Bala2: Bullets leave no SOUL. Only holes.
		Bala3: Gunpowder at dusk… and then, nothing. I eat the then.
	}

	Bioma: {
		Infierno1: The grimoire is hungry… and down here everything tastes of sulfur.
		Infierno2: Fire-flesh. Plenty. It burns the page.
		Infierno3: Even my mouth tastes of hell-salt.
		Mazmorra1: Old bones: the dungeon tastes of mold and broken promises.
		Mazmorra2: This tower's curse no longer feeds even its owners.
		Mazmorra3: Centuries-old skulls. Vintage, yes… but vintage.
		Corrupcion1: Corrupted flesh… bitter, but NOURISHING.
		Corrupcion2: This land bleeds purple. My favorite sauce.
		Corrupcion3: The eaters here taste of themselves. Food circle.
		Carmesi1: The crimson seeps. Better drunk than chewed.
		Carmesi2: Even the walls have a pulse here. Fresh.
		Carmesi3: They call this rain blood. I call it CLIMATE.
		Nieve1: The snow is quiet. Even the food is silent here.
		Nieve2: Frost on the palate: cold, slow, patient.
		Nieve3: The walking winter passed by here. Smells of Deerclops.
		Jungla1: Jungle flesh: green, juicy, full of thorns.
		Jungla2: The Queen's honey drips nearby. I can HEAR it.
		Jungla3: Spores, leaves, frenzy. This is eaten with both covers open.
		Desierto1: The desert only has dry bones and rattles.
		Desierto2: Sand between the pages. At least it CRUNCHES.
		Desierto3: The worms here bite back. Seasoning.
		Playa1: Salt, sand and crabs. A poor menu, but fresh.
		Playa2: The sea spits the food onto the shore. Table service.
		Playa3: Smells of fish and other people's treasures. Both are eaten.
		Sagrado1: Crystal sweetness… the hallow leaves an aftertaste of rainbow.
		Sagrado2: Even the light here is EDIBLE. Floating desserts.
		Sagrado3: Unicorns: the smuggest meat on the menu.
		Subsuelo1: Down here the food is gray, but plentiful.
		Subsuelo2: Damp caves: mushrooms, bats, echoes. I know about echoes.
		Subsuelo3: Stone keeps warmth and corpses. Both feed.
		Cielo1: The sky is light food. Barely fills a page.
		Cielo2: Floating islands: harpies with a view. MENU WITH A VIEW.
		Cielo3: Eating at altitude makes you dizzy… and hungry.
		Superficie1: The grimoire is hungry… and the surface is the buffet.
		Superficie2: Grass, zombies and night eyes. An everyday menu.
		Superficie3: The sun warms the meat up there. Come, let me taste it.
	}
}

